      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Monitoring procedures (Part I, line 2)</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>ANNUALLY THE FIRE FOUNDATION CONDUCTS 2 GRANT PROGRAMS WHERE ALL ELIGIBLE FIRE AGENCIES AND FIRE SAFE COUNCILS IN SAN DIEGO COUNTY CAN SUBMIT REQUESTS FOR EQUIPMENT FUNDING,TRAINING OR PREVENTION ACTIVITIES.THE FOUNDATION THEN SEEKS DONORS TO CONTRIBUTE AND FUND THESE APPLICATIONS.IF A DONOR SPECIFIES THEIR DONATION IS TO GO TO SPECIFIC GRANT REQUEST, THAT REQUEST IS HONORED.FOR ALL OTHER FUNDS WHERE THE DONOR HAS NOT MADE A SPECIFIC REQUEST TO FUND, THE FIRE FOUNDAITON BOARD PRIORITIZES REMAINING GRANT APPLICAITONS TO FUND AS MANY AS POSSIBLE.THE FIRE FOUNDATION REQUIRES ALL AGENCIES RECEIVING A GRANT TO SUPPLY RECEIPTS OR OTHER SUPPORTING EVIDENCE THAT THE GRANT FUNDS WERE EXPENDED AS SET FORTH IN THE GRANT.THE AGENCY WILL BE INELIGIBLE FOR FUTURE GRANTS IF IT FAILS TO PROVIDE DOCUMENTS.</ExplanationTxt>
